Technique C34: Using media queries to un-fixing sticky headers / footers - Example 1: Un-fix sticky headers / footers in HTML and CSS
The following example uses HTML and CSS to un-fix sticky headers / footers. The sticky regions get un-fixed as the height of the viewport is limited or the orientation is changed. When the min-height property matches the viewport space defined via media queries, regions which are not sticky get fixed or vice versa. This particular example uses the CSS min-height , max-height and min-width media query properties. <!DOCTYPE html > < html lang = "en" > < head > < meta charset = "UTF-8" > < title > Using media queries to un-fix sticky headers / footers </ title > < style > /* Sticky Styling */ header { min-height : 130px ; } @media ( min-height : 480px ) { header { position : -webkit-sticky; position : sticky; top : 0 ;
